  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 22p PM MDT WED AUG 26 2026 \nAn upper trough will bring cooler weather to the region over the\nweekend. A 20-50% chance of showers and lower probability of\nthunderstorms will cover Baker County in Oregon and much of SW\nIdaho on Saturday as the trough axis remains positioned to the\nwest. Breezy westerly winds behind Fridays cold front will bring\ngusts of 20-30 mph Saturday afternoon. Drier and cooler air \nmoves into the area on Sunday on the backside of the trough with\ngusty winds continuing across the Snake Plain. Temperatures are\nnear normal on Saturday, then drop to 5-10 degrees below normal\non Sunday, which puts lower elevations in the upper 70s. \nBrief ridging on Monday will keep dry conditions in place and \nbring a quick return to above normal temperatures. Models \ncontinue to advertise a progressive pattern for next week with \nanother trough moving through the Pac NW Tue/Wed. Moisture in \nadvance of this trough would favor a chance of \nshowers/thunderstorms across w-central/s-central Idaho zones on \nTuesday. Temperatures trend toward normal to slightly below \nnormal starting Tuesday.",
